---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../assets/personal/suleyman-portrait.jpg';
import '../../experiments/sk-character-studio/studio.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="SK Character Studio — Asset production pipeline" description="Isolated local GLB/glTF rig inspection, animation and character-production review. No finished character likeness is supplied." noindex>
<div class="sk-studio" data-studio>
<header class="sk-nav"><a href="/experiments/through-my-eyes/">SK / Character Studio</a><nav aria-label="Studio navigation"><a href="#studio-workbench">Viewer</a><a href="#production">Production brief</a><a href="/experiments/through-my-lens/">Phase 3 ↗</a></nav></header>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
<header class="sk-intro"><p class="sk-kicker">Phase 2 / Character production pipeline</p><h1>The asset makes<br/><em>the character.</em></h1><p>Load an artist-authored rig. Inspect its movement, materials and glasses fit before it enters the portfolio.</p><p class="sk-boundary">Production character not supplied. The existing non-likeness placeholder remains a fallback; it has not been polished or replaced.</p></header>
<section id="studio-workbench" class="sk-workbench" aria-labelledby="workbench-title">
<div class="sk-viewer" data-viewer><h2 id="workbench-title" class="sk-kicker">Asset review</h2><canvas data-studio-canvas aria-hidden="true"></canvas><figure class="sk-static"><Image src={portrait} alt="Unmodified reference photograph of Suleyman Koncagul wearing glasses" width={420} format="webp"/><figcaption>Original reference photograph · No live 3D rendering</figcaption></figure><p class="sk-asset-label" data-asset-label>Original reference view. Enable JavaScript and WebGL for rig inspection.</p></div>
<div class="sk-panel">
<div class="sk-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-status>Viewer not initialized. Production guidance and project links remain available.</div>
<fieldset data-runtime-controls disabled><legend>Asset source</legend><label class="sk-file">Choose local GLB / glTF bundle<input data-files type="file" multiple accept=".glb,.gltf,.bin,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.webp" aria-describedby="file-help"/></label><p id="file-help">Files stay in this browser. For .gltf, select its .bin and texture files together. 25 MiB maximum.</p><div class="sk-buttons"><button type="button" data-fixture>Load validation rig</button><button type="button" data-fallback>Use existing fallback</button></div><p class="sk-note">Validation rig = a skinned test strip with morphs. It is not character art or a likeness.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset data-runtime-controls disabled><legend>Motion</legend><div class="sk-buttons"><button type="button" data-pause aria-pressed="false">Pause animation</button><button type="button" data-reduce aria-pressed="false">Reduce motion</button></div><label>Animation clip<select data-clips disabled><option value="">No imported clips</option></select></label><label class="sk-checkbox"><input type="checkbox" data-tracking checked/>Head and eye tracking</label><label>Head direction<input data-yaw type="range" min="-1" max="1" step=".01" value="0"/></label><div class="sk-gaze"><label>Gaze horizontal<input data-gaze-x type="range" min="-1" max="1" step=".01" value="0"/></label><label>Gaze vertical<input data-gaze-y type="range" min="-1" max="1" step=".01" value="0"/></label></div><button type="button" data-blink disabled>Blink preview</button></fieldset>
<fieldset data-runtime-controls disabled><legend>Camera</legend><div class="sk-buttons"><button type="button" data-front>Front view</button><button type="button" data-close>Head close-up</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset view</button></div><label>View angle<input data-orbit type="range" min="-60" max="60" step="1" value="0"/></label><label>Camera distance<input data-zoom type="range" min=".65" max="1.5" step=".01" value="1"/></label></fieldset>
<details><summary>Facial and material inspection</summary><fieldset data-runtime-controls disabled><legend>Morph targets</legend><label>Target<select data-morphs disabled><option value="">No imported morphs</option></select></label><label>Influence<input data-morph-value type="range" min="0" max="1" step=".01" value="0" disabled/></label><button type="button" data-clear-morph disabled>Clear morph preview</button><h3>Materials</h3><label>Material<select data-materials disabled><option value="">No imported materials</option></select></label><label>Roughness<input data-roughness type="range" min="0" max="1" step=".01" value=".5" disabled/></label><label>Metalness<input data-metalness type="range" min="0" max="1" step=".01" value="0" disabled/></label><button type="button" data-restore-material disabled>Restore authored material</button><p class="sk-note">Preview overrides affect this loaded instance only. Texture maps and original files are preserved.</p></fieldset></details>
</div></section>
<section class="sk-report" aria-labelledby="report-title"><p class="sk-kicker">Asset inspection / capabilities, not visual approval</p><h2 id="report-title">What actually loaded.</h2><pre data-report>Awaiting viewer initialization.</pre><p class="sk-note" data-performance>No runtime measurements yet.</p></section>
<section id="production" class="sk-production" aria-labelledby="production-title"><p class="sk-kicker">Production handoff</p><h2 id="production-title">Build the likeness.<br/><em>Then judge the movement.</em></h2><div class="sk-production-grid"><div><h3>Reference first</h3><p>Neutral front, both profiles and both three-quarter views. Consistent lighting, camera height and hairstyle. Include glasses on/off and the intended clothing.</p><p>No missing proportions should be invented from the one existing photograph.</p></div><div><h3>Artist-approved asset</h3><p>A modeled head and upper body, fitted glasses socket, deforming skeleton, independent eyes, blink morphs and a restrained Idle clip. Inspect the neutral model before animating it.</p></div><div><h3>Acceptance is visual, too</h3><p>Correct loading is not character approval. Review silhouette, face, hair, neck, collar, expression and materials at desktop and mobile scale.</p></div></div><p>Blender guide, rig naming contract, photo checklist and design brief are provided with the local source handoff.</p></section>
</main><footer class="sk-footer"><span>Isolated production tool / Nothing uploaded or deployed</span><a href="/experiments/through-my-eyes/">Return to character experiment ↗</a><a href="/">Portfolio ↗</a></footer>
</div>
<script>import '../../experiments/sk-character-studio/viewer';</script>
</BaseLayout>
